      "summaries": {
        "en": "Hummingbot is an open-source framework for building and deploying algorithmic trading bots in cryptocurrency markets, addressing the need for automated, high-frequency trading strategies accessible to developers and traders. Its technical strength lies in modular architecture using Python and Cython, enabling custom strategy development with real-time market data processing and exchange connectivity. Users can implement arbitrage, market-making, or trend-following strategies across centralized and decentralized exchanges, with backtesting capabilities to validate approaches before live deployment.",
        "zh": "Hummingbot是一个开源框架，专门用于构建和部署加密货币市场的算法交易机器人，解决了开发者和交易者对自动化高频交易策略的需求。其技术核心采用Python和Cython的模块化架构，允许用户开发自定义策略，实时处理市场数据并连接多个交易所。通过该工具，您可以实现套利、做市或趋势跟踪等策略，支持中心化和去中心化交易平台，并具备回测功能以验证策略有效性，适合想要探索自动化交易或研究市场微观结构的实践者。",
        "es": "Hummingbot is an open-source framework for building and deploying algorithmic trading bots in cryptocurrency markets, addressing the need for automated, high-frequency trading strategies accessible to developers and traders. Its technical strength lies in modular architecture using Python and Cython, enabling custom strategy development with real-time market data processing and exchange connectivity. Users can implement arbitrage, market-making, or trend-following strategies across centralized and decentralized exchanges, with backtesting capabilities to validate approaches before live deployment.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "hummingbot stands out for algotrading, arbitrage, and backtesting in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Hummingbot is an open-source framework for building and deploying algorithmic trading bots in cryptocurrency markets, addressing the need for automated, high-frequency trading strategies accessible to developers and traders. Its technical strength lies in modular architecture using Python and Cython, enabling custom strategy development with real-time market data processing and exchange connectivity. Users can implement arbitrage, market-making, or trend-following strategies across centralized and decentralized exchanges, with backtesting capabilities to validate approaches before live deployment.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/hummingbot/hummingbot for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
