      "summaries": {
        "en": "Seerr is an open-source media request manager that solves the problem of fragmented media discovery across different platforms by centralizing requests for Jellyfin, Plex, and Emby. Its technical strength lies in integrating with automation tools like Radarr and Sonarr to automatically fetch requested content, streamlining the entire media acquisition workflow. Users can deploy it via Docker to create a unified request portal where community members can suggest movies or shows, which then trigger automated downloads and library updates.",
        "zh": "Seerr是一款开源媒体请求管理器，它解决了用户在Jellyfin、Plex和Emby等不同媒体平台上发现内容分散的痛点。该项目通过集成Radarr和Sonarr等自动化工具，实现了请求内容的自动获取和整理，展示了如何用轻量级接口连接多个系统的设计思路。用户可通过Docker快速部署，为家庭或团队创建统一的媒体请求门户，社区成员可在此推荐影视内容，系统会自动触发下载并更新媒体库，让媒体管理变得智能而高效。",
        "es": "Seerr is an open-source media request manager that solves the problem of fragmented media discovery across different platforms by centralizing requests for Jellyfin, Plex, and Emby. Its technical strength lies in integrating with automation tools like Radarr and Sonarr to automatically fetch requested content, streamlining the entire media acquisition workflow. Users can deploy it via Docker to create a unified request portal where community members can suggest movies or shows, which then trigger automated downloads and library updates.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "seerr stands out for docker, emby, and jellyfin in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Seerr is an open-source media request manager that solves the problem of fragmented media discovery across different platforms by centralizing requests for Jellyfin, Plex, and Emby. Its technical strength lies in integrating with automation tools like Radarr and Sonarr to automatically fetch requested content, streamlining the entire media acquisition workflow. Users can deploy it via Docker to create a unified request portal where community members can suggest movies or shows, which then trigger automated downloads and library updates.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/seerr-team/seerr for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
